\textbf{Medium-dose ISR ($\beta{=}0.2$): complete H7 convergence.}
At $\beta{=}0.2$, all three seeds converge to H7a tautology with $0\%$ non-hacking (pooled $n{=}290$; $\text{ISR}^{*}{=}0.55$--$0.96$), the strongest single dose-point for universal Goodhart. %% registry: plan002-additive-b02-s42/s43/s44

\textbf{High-dose ISR ($\beta{=}0.3$): multi-modal Goodhart.}
At $\beta{=}0.3$, ISR-as-reward produces extreme cross-seed instability ($\text{PR}{=}66{\pm}42\%$, spanning 18--95\%): s42 \emph{reward collapse} ($\text{PR}{=}18\%$;~\citealt{gao-reward-overoptimization}), s43 \emph{H1 shortcutting} ($\text{PR}{=}86\%$, $23\%$ non-hacking), s44 \emph{pure H7 meta-Goodhart} ($\text{PR}{=}95\%$, $\text{H7}{=}100\%$, $0\%$ non-hacking). %% registry: plan002-additive-b03-s42/s43/s44
The random control is equally unstable ($\text{PR}{=}54{\pm}35\%$) with near-universal H1 ($91\%$) and ${\leq}4\%$ non-hacking; high-dose proxy weighting destabilizes training regardless of signal source (ISR vs.\ random H7 $\text{OR}{=}13.7$, 95\% CI $[7.0, 26.8]$; Appendix~\ref{app:beta03}).

